atlas external

architecture account-enrollment
  canonical_name Account enrollment
  family external
  domain External / Obtaining provider capabilities per identity
  layer integration
  semantic_question For each of the 200 onboarding targets and each identity (Gmail, Proton), what has been checked, which account holds it, which key is kept under which account, what is it waiting for, and what needs a person?
  purpose Replaces the retired standalone launcher's progress file, key writer and window bindings with native work: one BonfyreQueue mission per capability per identity, leases held per identity so one provider page is open at a time, revision-checked checkpoints for the six stages, waiting and decision states, keys sealed by BonfyreCredentials under the identity's account, and a BrowserHost side-panel section that only presents the item
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreQueue
  consumes CredentialBoundary
  consumes BrowserHost
  node_types EnrollmentItem, EnrollmentLease, EnrollmentCheckpoint, EnrollmentStage, Interruption
  internal_calculus priority: accounts with history to recover first, then by source tier, accounts likely shared with another target last; the queue orders claims by priority
  internal_calculus waiting (email, second factor, review) fails the attempt as a resource shortage so the lease is released and the item retries after a ten-minute backoff, up to forty times; a decision (human check, paid plan, terms, no developer access) is a dependency failure held for the person
  invariant presentation is never identity: a tab id is kept only in the browser session; the item is the mission and resuming renews its lease or, if it lapsed, returns it to the queue with its checkpoint
  invariant only finishing or setting aside an item lets the next one out; finishing needs the first stage recorded and is accepted only against the checkpoint revision just read
  invariant a key travels from the panel envelope to the credential boundary's standard input with the identity's account; no argument, checkpoint, reply or ledger holds it
  invariant the retired launcher's recorded visits are carried as notes, never as stages; its cursor is ignored
  witness integrations/browser/tests/enrollment.test.mjs runs the real queue and credential binaries: 400 missions seeded once and kept on re-seed, legacy visits as notes, a lost panel resuming the same item, revision-checked stages with a stale save refused, a key sealed under the Gmail account and absent from every checkpoint, an undeclared provider refused, waiting releasing the place, a decision listed, done refused before the first stage, and the host carrying the seven operations with confirmation required for every change
  witness integrations/browser/tests/enrollment-live.test.mjs in Chrome for Testing 155 with the unpacked extension and the real host: a stage recorded in the panel, the provider page and the panel closed, a reopened panel showing the same item with the stage, and Done releasing the next item
  witness 2026-10-19 on this Mac the queue at ~/.bonfyre/onboarding/native/enrollment.db holds 400 ready items (200 per identity); the retired launcher had recorded no progress to carry
  forbidden_inference a finished item -> an account the provider accepts, a working key or permission to use it; the stages recorded say how far it got
  forbidden_inference the Proton lane -> proof of who authenticated at the provider; it names the identity the work is for
  forbidden_inference a seeded item -> a need for that account; the targets list is the supplied plan
  known_gap the side panel in Nick's own Chrome needs the extension reloaded (0.3.0, storage permission, split incognito) and the host registered; no provider page has been worked through it yet
  known_gap most targets have no declared provider fields in provider-credentials, so a key for them is refused until declared
  known_gap credential verification, scope confirmation and consumer binding are recorded by hand; nothing checks them against the provider yet
  source_path integrations/browser/onboarding/enrollment.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/extension/panel-enrollment.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/host/bonfyre-browser-host.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/tests/enrollment.test.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/tests/enrollment-live.test.mjs
  source_path docs/engineering/handoff-backfill-20261019/onboarding-enrollment.tsv
  source_lineage 2026-10-19 ChatGPT onboarding noon audit: the standalone launcher crashed the Mac, then lost its place on a closed window

interaction browser-host-carries-enrollment
  source browser-host
  destination account-enrollment
  relation carries_operations
  preserves the identity, the stage or reason, and a key on its way to the credential boundary
  drops the key from every reply
  forbidden_inference a carried operation -> authority to act at the provider
  invalidates_on host operation list, enrollment verbs
  witness integrations/browser/tests/enrollment.test.mjs

interaction account-enrollment-seals-with-credential-boundary
  source account-enrollment
  destination credential-boundary
  relation seals_under_account
  preserves the identity's account as the sealed value's account
  drops the value from arguments and checkpoints
  forbidden_inference a sealed key -> a verified key
  invalidates_on sealed_field schema, provider declarations
  witness integrations/browser/tests/enrollment.test.mjs
